# Repo-root scratch directory: throwaway diagnostics, previews, one-off scripts.
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose — a bare `tmp/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which is the failure mode both NBs at the foot of this file describe.
# Nothing under tmp/ was tracked when this was added (checked with `git ls-files`).
/tmp/

# Local cleanup notes (delete once committed)
CHANGELOG_CLEANUP.md
CLEANUP_PROPOSAL.md
inventory.json

# NB: agent context is split into two tiers (decision 2026-07-27, superseding the
# machine-local-only decision of 2026-07-26):
#   TRACKED (shared with collaborators, other machines, and both Claude Code and Codex):
#     AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .agents/skills/, docs/agent-context/, scripts/
#   IGNORED (this machine only):
#     CLAUDE.local.md  — absolute paths, shell quirks
#     .claude/         — settings.json, open-questions.md, _archive/, and the
#                        skills/ mirror generated by scripts/sync_agent_skills.py
# Do not widen `CLAUDE.local.md` back to `CLAUDE*`: that would untrack CLAUDE.md, and a
# fresh clone would then have no file importing AGENTS.md for Claude Code.
# See main/.claude/_archive/agent-context-migration-2026-07-27/MIGRATION.md.

# NB: the Python-packaging block near the top of this file matches on BASENAME AT ANY
# DEPTH, exactly like `data*` and the `*cache*` rule below. That makes several obvious
# directory names unusable anywhere in the tree, silently:
#     report/lib/…    analysis/lib/…    -> excluded by `lib/`
#     report/parts/…                    -> excluded by `parts/`
#     report/build/…                    -> excluded by `build/`
#     anything/env/…  anything/var/…    -> excluded by `env/`, `var/`
# `report/lib/` is the natural name for a shared report library and would have been the
# third instance of this failure. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` before choosing
# `report/render/` instead. Before creating any new tracked directory, run:
#     git check-ignore -v <path>
# Trackable alternatives already checked: report/render/, report/assets/, report/blocks/,
# analysis/common/, docs/experiments/, utils/run_context.py.
# Do NOT "fix" this by adding negations for each name -- git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, which is the same constraint that puts
# docs/results_index.md in docs/ rather than under results/.

# NB: do NOT add a blanket `*cache*` rule here. It silently untracked 23 files
# (2.3 MB), 18 of them the `cache_*.csv` in figures_for_paper/*/source_data/ that
# README.md designates as shipped paper source data, plus the panels_cache_*.npz
# that semantic_regression_panels.py reads to render its figures. Because those
# caches determine the rendered output but were invisible to git, they drifted
# out of sync with the committed figures without anything showing up in
# `git status`. The two caches that genuinely should be ignored -- __pycache__/
# and .vector_cache -- are already listed explicitly above.

# NB: `data*` is the same kind of blanket rule and it has already bitten once. It is
# meant for the raw-data tree, but it matches on basename at any depth, so creating
# docs/agent-context/data-conventions.md on 2026-07-28 produced a file that existed on
# disk, resolved every route pointing at it, and was invisible to git -- untracked in a
# directory the whole two-tier scheme above declares TRACKED. Codex and a fresh clone
# would simply not have had it. Hence the explicit `!` negation next to the rule.
# The negation works only because no parent directory is excluded; the same trick is
# impossible under `*results`, which is why docs/results_index.md lives in docs/.
# Before adding any file whose name starts with `data` to a tracked directory, run
# `git check-ignore -v <path>`. scripts/validate_agent_config.py now checks this.
